## 2. Ground-truth the bench — recorded state is always stale

Run these before planning anything. **Never trust a `.setup` file, a memory, or this document
for any of it.**

```bash
# Which unit is on which console — the .setup has had these REVERSED
show system            # serial number AND "Bootloader version :" (see §1 — WHICH BUILD?)
show stack             # stack state CHURNS between sessions
show boot              # boot image, backup, and Boot Security Level
dir *.rel              # does the release the suite needs actually exist
show file systems      # is flash empty (a prior erase/flash-test case leaves it so)
```

**Check the console baud before anything else.** The `.setup` pins `9600`, which is the factory
default — but the rate is a *stored bootloader setting* (Boot Menu option 4), so a bench can be
left at 115200 and the suite then cannot talk to the DUT at all. A mismatched rate looks like a
dead console: a bare CR returns a handful of garbage bytes, not silence. Sweep 9600/115200 and
pick the one that yields printable output. Boot Menu option 7 reverts it to 9600, announces the
change, and **waits for you to follow it down** before continuing.

Four failure modes that present as something else:

- **A destacked unit keeps its old stack ID.** Its whole `port1.0.x` range goes phantom
  (`Provisioned`, MAC `0000.0000.0000`) while the real ports are `port2.0.x`. Config naming the
  phantom ports is **accepted silently**. This once presented as a DHCP option-61 defect that
  did not exist.
- **A non-`none` Boot Security Level locks out 2002, 2003 and 2005 alike** — the framework has no
  bootloader-password handling. Clearing it **erases the flash filesystem**, so it needs a
  re-image plan, not just a menu selection.
- **Empty flash is normal after an erase/flash-test case** and means the DUT netboots from the
  testbox's TFTP. It will not boot if that testbox stops serving.
- **The bootloader-side link is only up DURING BOOT.** Testbox-side carrier is *not* a valid
  pre-flight check — a working path looks identical to an unplugged one until the DUT
  power-cycles.

Bench identities as of **2026-08-11** — verify, do not assume. The `.setup` file has had these
two **reversed**, so confirm by serial number before driving either console:

| Bench | Console | S/N | PDU |
|---|---|---|---|
| tb470 | `/dev/u4` | 264A23052 | 10.36.150.14 outlet 4 ("D") |
| tb470 | `/dev/u5` | 264A23066 | 10.36.150.14 outlet 5 ("E") |

**tb504 is OUT OF SCOPE.** It is a shared testbox outside our control. Do not target it, do not
plan a run on it, and do not propose it as a second bench — even though earlier IE520 work
(the 2026-08-07/08 baseline campaign and the suite 2005 runs) happened there. Historical results
from it remain valid evidence; the bench itself is not ours to use.

Never cable ports 27/28 between the two tb470 IE520s — same chassis-id `3039` = duplicate-master.
Only `10.38.215.0/24` has an upstream return path and tb470 has **no NAT**.

