## 4. Measured timings — never extrapolate these

**Operations on this platform run LONGER than linear.** Do not size a budget from an `n/50`
progress counter on a run that timed out — that is exactly how the too-small budgets got there,
and it produced false failures on operations that were working correctly.

| Operation | Real cost | Budget | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Security level 2→1 erase | **2143 s** measured end-to-end | 3000 s | Correct. Original 780 s covered 36%, so the framework power-cycled the DUT mid-erase and the level never cleared — which locked that unit out of the boot menu entirely, with no way back in (no framework password handling). |
| Security level 3→1 erase | **2150 s** measured | 3000 s | Agrees with the above within 7 s → reproducible, not load-dependent. |
| Stage-2 Erase FLASH | ~27 min | 3000 s | Correct; passes. Was never failing — the old 1200 s ceiling cut it off at 36/50 blocks. |
| Stage-2 Test FLASH | **~9300 s per test, ~18,600 s for both** | 10800 s | **Still short.** Needs ~21,000 s. Currently fails by the clock with test 1/2 device-reported PASS. |
| YMODEM one-off boot | ~12 h at 9600 | — | 2002 case 113 excluded by `testCaseRunPriority = 10`. Never exercised. |

`waitTime` is a **ceiling** — `send()` returns as soon as `strList` matches — so a generous value
costs nothing on a healthy run. There is no reason to be stingy.

