## 8. Load the memories, then check what's actually open

```bash
ls claude/Test-cases/.claude/memory/*.md      # the directory IS the list
```

Read `MEMORY.md` (the index) and then the files whose hooks match today's work. The IE520 and
bench ones are the relevant cluster; `x230v2-5700-control-corpus` carries §1 in full. Memories are
symlinked from `~/.claude/projects/*/memory`, so the same set loads from either directory. **Any
memory name written down — including here — is a hint, not a guarantee.** A memory reflects what
was true when written; if it names a file, flag or unit, confirm that still exists.

**Open threads rot — verify each against the logs and the tree before reporting it as open.**
As of 2026-08-12:

- **D1/D5 — the release-verification question for the bootloader team.** Highest value, and now
  **narrowed to one concrete ask** by the 2026-08-12 pauld-build test: the U-Boot suppression is
  done and correct; what is missing is the AT status message layer on both paths —
  `Verifying release... OK` (success) and `Error: This release file is not intended for this
  device.` (failure). Until that lands, every case that passes only via a widened boot marker is
  **unverified**, not passed.
- **`BOOT_MARKERS` needs revising for the pauld build** — 3 of 4 markers are dead there; only
  `login:` survives. `Mounting` / `Initializing` are present and are what the RCA originally
  recommended. Not yet changed in the tree.
- **`Bootloader version : pauld`** — 2002 case 70 asserts the bootloader version appears in system
  information, and is now comparing against a developer name.
- **Case 30's `testCaseMethod` says "one off TFTP boot"** but the code omits `source`, so it
  defaults to `'flash'` and `configure()` pre-stages the file there. Documented method and actual
  behaviour disagree.
- **2003 case 10 (Test FLASH)** — needs ~21,000 s, and discards test 1/2's device-reported PASS.
  Asserting per-test banks that coverage even when the clock beats it.
- **The bootloader escape has never fired on hardware** — insurance, not a dependency, and unproven.
- **`Error, no UBI device selected!`** in 2002.110/120 — pre-existing, so not caused by any fix.
  If it survives a run with the `Saving settings` fix in place it becomes a second product question.
- **2002 case 113 (YMODEM)** unexercised — needs a standalone run; not viable at 9600.
- **Suite 2005 has only ever run on tb504**, which is now out of scope. Running it on a tb470 IE520
  is new ground: budget for it, expect first-run surprises, and note that its flash-erasing cases
  will leave that unit netboot-dependent (§6). Its one open failure there was a framework abort —
  `dut.mode('#')` hitting the flat 1800 s timeout during a dark SPIFlash write, not a product fault.
  There is also no after-action document for 2005.
- **Diagnostics menu option 8** — absent from both IE520 menus while Ctrl+U still reaches U-Boot.
  Terrence's call, 2026-08-12: it has been removed for a while and **does not count** as a finding.
  Out of scope; do not re-raise it as a defect.

